            <ArticleTitle>State-dependent pain in winter depression.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>672-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The incidence and nature of state-dependent pain were investigated in 43 consecutively presenting patients with recurrent autumn/winter episodes of major depression followed by spontaneous recovery in the spring. Twenty-two (51.2%) experienced state-dependent pain, which appears to be a common concomitant of wintertime depression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
